  "notes": "Mae Fah Luang University’s Chiang Rai database and Tourism Authority records describe the characteristic low Chiang Saen gable, nine overlapping gilded stupa tiers, one-storey timber Jade Hall and two-storey teak-clad museum. Three original creator-released images document the stupa, ordination hall’s porch and the museum’s teak and gilding."
